==================================================
28. KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
==================================================

1. SVR = Support Vector Regression.

2. It is a supervised learning algorithm for CONTINUOUS
   target prediction.

3. It is based on the Support Vector Machine concept.

4. Its central idea is the ε-insensitive tube.

5. Errors within ε receive no loss.

6. Errors outside ε are penalized.

7. Important training points are called support vectors.

8. C controls the penalty for violations.

9. ε controls the width of the tolerance tube.

10. Gamma controls the locality of influence for kernels
    such as RBF.

11. Kernels allow SVR to model nonlinear relationships.

12. RBF is a commonly used nonlinear kernel.

13. Feature scaling is generally IMPORTANT for SVR.

14. Important hyperparameters:

    C
    epsilon
    kernel
    gamma

15. Main intuition:

    DATA
      ↓
    ε-TUBE
      ↓
    SUPPORT VECTORS
      ↓
    OPTIMIZATION
      ↓
    PREDICTION